  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">222226_Global Fund Somalia TB - GC7</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Global Fund Somalia TB - Grant Cycle 7. This is a programme continuation from GC6 (formerly known in GF terminology as NFM4), and the next funding cycle of the Global Fund programme which is renewed every three years. World Vision Somalia and UK have partnered (SO-FO) to be Principal Recipients since 2009.
 
 The Global Fund TB programme funds provides the funding for the TB programme in Somalia on behalf of the Ministry of Health, given that the Government of Somalia has scarce resources to support the programme.
 
 Working with 7 Sub-Recipients (including iNGOs, local NGOs, and the provincial MoHs) throughout Somalia and Somaliland, the Global Fund grant has expanded its coverage bringing diagnostic and treatment closer to the most vulnerable populations. To date there are 110+ TB medical centres across the country.
 
 The leadership of Somalias Global Fund TB Tuberculosis program in conjunction with the Somalias National Tuberculosis Program (NTP) has seen the case notification rate increase 16,918 in 2019 to 18,722 in 2022, despite an estimated decline in prevalence rate (the rate at which the disease circulates in the country. A prevalence survey has not been conducted since 2011 and thus prevalence is estimated by WHO through proxy indicators); and in the same period the treatment success rate (TSR) increased from 87% to 94%, thus remaining above the WHO recommended TSR of 85% for new and relapse cases.
 
 The SO-FO pairing carries an expectation of Match on the grant. For the 2024-2026 cycle, an amount of $950,196.94 has been agreed with WV Somalia. ICR &amp; DPC is estimated at 5% of &amp;#163;27m = $1,373,726</narrative>
  </description>
